A||N||12||87ECO5||Can these prices be beat?||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||01-18-2001||12:37 PM||||I'm about to sink some major $$$ into suspension components for my coupe and wanted to get some feedback from my PFF buddies.<P>I've been maintaining a spreadsheet for about 2 months now - a living, breathing document that's been molded and shaped over the last few weeks to include best prices I've found for the components I want.<P>Below are those components, the vendors supplying them and the prices I was either quoted or found on their websites.  If you have a few moments to spare, please look over the list and let me know if you're aware of a place that offers better prices.  Please note - these prices DO NOT include shipping charges.<P>.<P><B>Eibach performance springs</B> (Pro-kit, 1" drop) from  <A HREF="http://Shox.com" TARGET=_blank>Shox.com</A>  - $219.00<BR><B>KYB shocks/struts</B> from  <A HREF="http://Shox.com" TARGET=_blank>Shox.com</A>  - $199.00<BR><B>Steering damper</B> from  <A HREF="http://FieroStore.com" TARGET=_blank>FieroStore.com</A>  - $40.42<BR><B>Complete poly suspension kit</B> from  <A HREF="http://Suspension.com" TARGET=_blank>Suspension.com</A>  (includes front and rear control arm bushings, front sway bar frame bushings and endlinks, engine cradle mounts, TRS bushings, poly tie rod end boots, front upper and lower ball joints, front outer tie rod ends, rear lower ball joints and rear outer tie rod ends) - $340.00<BR><B>Konig Monsoons</B> (17x7, 5-100/114 40S) from  <A HREF="http://WhalenTire.com" TARGET=_blank>WhalenTire.com</A>  - $530/set<BR><B>Kumho ECTSA Supra 712</B> (225/45R17, Z-rated) from  <A HREF="http://WhalenTire.com" TARGET=_blank>WhalenTire.com</A>  - $404.00<BR><B>Strut tower brace</B> from Darrell Morse - $120.00<BR><B>Addco front and rear sway bars</B> from  <A HREF="http://Shox.com" TARGET=_blank>Shox.com</A>  - $129.00/each<P>Thanks for your time.<p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cheever2||01-18-2001||12:40 PM||||Wow.  Do that for all Fiero parts and put it on a website.<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||Old Lar||01-18-2001||12:52 PM||||List all that out and you'll be depressed on how much you are spending.  You've got over $2000 in just those parts.  If you do all the labor that saves another $2000.<P>Those Fiero's are expensive little toys to reconstruct.  I don't know what other places charge for those components, so I'm no help at all.<P>||||reg||3
Z||000003||ChadMan||01-18-2001||01:01 PM||||You make a very good point, Larry.  <P>There comes a time in every Fieroholic's life when s/he has to decide if s/he wants to sink two or three grand into a car that Kelley Blue Book says is worth less than that!  It's a leap of faith.<P>I have stood at the abyss for over a year now, afraid to spend the money on an engine swap for the Coupe.  Scott, I admire your courage and hope I will have the sack to follow in your footsteps.<P>"Only in the leap from the lion's head will he prove his worth."  Dr. Henry Jones, 'Indiana Jones and the Last Crusade'||||reg||1
Z||000004||87ECO5||01-18-2001||01:12 PM||||No book can tell what this car is worth to <B>me</B>.  You just can't put a price on that.  It goes much deeper ...<P>That's what makes me an idio ... I mean, a Fieroholic!       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by 87ECO5 (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000005||kinboyatuwo||01-18-2001||02:01 PM||||cheers to that 87eco5<P>all in favour<BR>say I<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."||||reg||1
Z||000006||firstfiero||01-18-2001||02:05 PM||||     Well Said!!!||||reg||6
Z||000007||bHooper||01-18-2001||02:29 PM||||Scott, <P>take a look at my list from last month.  i have part numbers, prices and source's... some things appear to be much cheaper than you have listed.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004682.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/004682.html</A> <P>also the steering stabilizer is available from most autoparts stores for much less than what the fiero store charges.<P>hope this helps!<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||01-18-2001||02:30 PM||||You can save $40 and just scrap the steering damper.<BR>There was a thread about that a couple of weeks ago.<BR>You can save another $120 by not buying the strut tower brace. It's not really necessary.<BR>Then you can take the $160 you just saved and buy adjustable Konis instead of KYB's.<BR>Admittedly, it's not my money, but that's how I would spend it.<P>Have you checked to make sure that your outer tie-rod ends are actually in need of replacement? I have replaced all four front ball joints on two Fieros, but have not yet seen an outer tie-rod end in need of it.<BR>1FST2M6 can tell you where to get cheap p-urethane ($20 for rear kit, $30 for cradle I think).<BR>Front ball joints with a lifetime warranty can be had from Autozone for ~$75 for all four.<BR>If you buy a larger front bar, you can engineer your stock front bar onto the rear and save ~$120.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||01-18-2001||02:57 PM||||Those look good. Just a few things, Tell the Fiero store you belong to a Fiero Club and you'll get 10% off. (so the dampener is $36) I also noticed that you don't list the rear sway bar hardware (bushings and endlinks). If I remember correctly the Addco's do not come with mounting hardware just the bars. So you could get the rear sway bar from the Fiero store for $135 and it comes with all the hardware. (it's $150 -10% = $135) The price for the suspension kit with all the bushings and mounts looks great!<P>BTW ~ I added up the springs,shocks,struts, and sway bars. Total is $676.00 + shipping. The Fiero Store KYB kit #2 is $680. But with the 10% discount it's $612 and my receipt shows $44 for shipping. So the total with shipping was $656.00.<P>Fiero Store KYB Kit #2 is:<BR>KYB struts and shocks<BR>Eibach 1" lowering springs<BR>Suspension Tech Sway Bars with poly bushings and endlinks.<P>As for value of the car, once you do a lot of stuff to the car (suspension, engine, paint, etc) You can have it appraised fro it true value and insure it as such. My car is insured as a "classic" and insured for it's appraised value. Which is much higher than the standard value.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||2xsess||01-18-2001||05:15 PM||||1FST2M6 says that NOPIs prices on the poly bsushings are way cheaper, I haven't compared yet as I'm not up to that stage.<P><B>Nopi Poly bushings part numbers and pricing</B><P><BR>7-304 is the Rear Control Arm kit, $18.87<BR>7-502 Cradle mount's, $32.37<BR>7-207 Front Control Arm kit, $32.37<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My_car_(large)sig_1.JPG">   <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||fiero56||01-18-2001||10:06 PM||||The problem with NOPI is that I haven't heard one positive plug for them other than from Travis. I called them, got some moron on the line, didn't sound like he even knew where he was. WT3 ordered before Thanksgiving, still hasn't seen any of his stuff, and it's half way through January. I think Hooper ordered from them, but didn't hear how it turned out. That, and the kit from suspension.com comes with all bushings, balljoints, tie-rod ends, etc, etc. Yes, his tie-rod ends are bad, along with ball joints, etc. <BR>Koni's are wast of money(IMO) if the car is mostly for the street. How many of you Koni owners actually adjust them after the initial settings? I agree about ditching the steering damper. Forget the lowering springs and get drop spindles.<P>suspension.com kit:<BR>Front & rear control arm bushings, front sway bar frame & endlinks, engine cradle mounts,  <BR>engine strut torque(dogbone) bushings, poly tie rod end boots,  <BR>Front upper & lower ball joints, front outer tie rod ends,  <BR>rear lower ball joints and rear outer tie rod ends.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-18-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||bHooper||01-19-2001||04:39 PM||||ok, ok... i'll admit it!<P><BR><B>I had a good NOPI experience!</B><P>yes, they are morons, that only seem to know about Jap cars, but if you have a part number, they can work with that.<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
